/** @defgroup bflat_ts_exception_handler bflat build - managed exception handling
 * @ingroup bflat_ts
 * @{
 *
 * @brief Tests managed exception-handling semantics (try/catch/finally,
 *        filters, rethrow, unwinding) and the routing of an unhandled managed
 *        `throw` into a C# handler instead of a blind fail-fast.
 *
 *        The eh_* tests pin standard .NET EH behavior: catch by exact and
 *        base type, catch/finally ordering on both paths, multi-frame
 *        unwinding with intermediate finallys, exception filters, rethrow and
 *        InnerException, runtime-raised exceptions (divide-by-zero, bounds,
 *        invalid cast, checked overflow, null dereference), and that a CAUGHT
 *        exception is never diverted into the ZkvmThrow handler.
 *
 *        A managed throw lowers to RhpThrowEx, which bflat redirects with
 *        --wrap=RhpThrowEx to rhp's __wrap_RhpThrowEx. That wrapper forwards the
 *        exception object (a0) to a weak symbol `ZkvmThrow` that a program may
 *        export via [UnmanagedCallersOnly]; the handler receives the live
 *        Exception and terminates the guest.
 *
 *        Exercises the full chain that makes this work in the zkVM:
 *        - exception object forwarding in __wrap_RhpThrowEx
 *        - no-op RhpReversePInvoke (so a managed handler can be entered from the
 *          throw path without trapping on a GC rendezvous)
 *        - exit() override emitting the Zisk exit ecall (a7=93) so the guest
 *          terminates cleanly instead of EmulationNoCompleted
 *
 * @}
 */
